# Commits of upstream's that are later than the one in UPSTREAM_REF and that
# the fork carries anyway, one to a line, in the order they're applied. The
# proof applies each of them to upstream before it builds it, so the fork is
# compared with upstream as it is with those commits and no others.
#
# This is for a fix that upstream has made and hasn't released in the version
# the fork is based on, where upstream without the fix can't be compared with
# anything, the fork included, because what it does varies from run to run.
# Each line is a claim that the commit is upstream's own, which anyone can
# check against github.com/hashicorp/terraform, and each is recorded in the
# report. Take a line out when UPSTREAM_REF moves to a version that has it.
#
# Adding a line is a decision for a person. See proposals/workflows.
